{
  "description": "Shared conditional-semantics vector suite (bd polyglot-pdf-h76m.1, P0.1). Pins TODAY'S show_if evaluation semantics of BOTH evaluators -- the voice runtime (frontend/src/schema-forms/utils/validation.ts shouldShowField) and the editor preview (schema-editor/src/utils/conditionalVisibility.ts shouldShowField) -- BEFORE the schema-v2 composite-logic rework changes anything. This file is the anti-drift contract: any semantic change must be made in both evaluators AND here, deliberately, or CI turns red. Includes the vq4m equals-as-membership hack on checkbox-group triggers, the comma-string gating (voice path), and known warts (String() coercions, no trim on is_empty). Do not 'fix' an expectation to make a code change pass -- a red runner means the evaluators and this contract disagree, which is exactly the drift this suite exists to catch.",
  "expectShape": "expect is either a boolean (both evaluators agree -- the normal case) or {frontend, editor} (a field shape where the two evaluators GENUINELY DIVERGE today; pinned honestly rather than papered over). Divergences stem from the comma-split gate: the runtime keys on group_kind === 'checkbox', the editor keys on type === 'checkbox' with non-empty options[] (its FormField type has no group_kind). The editor also never unwraps FieldValue objects (a runtime storage detail).",
  "normalizeShape": "The `normalize` section (bd h76m.7, P3.0) pins normalizeToComposite -- the shape-only coexistence contract duplicated verbatim in frontend/src/schema-forms/utils/normalizeToComposite.ts and schema-editor/src/utils/normalizeToComposite.ts. Each case is {name, input?, expect}: input omitted means undefined; expect is the canonical composite group or null (null = 'always shown', which is also the FAIL-OPEN result for every malformed shape -- those cases also emit a console.warn). Normalize NEVER rewrites operators or values; semantics stay in the leaf evaluators until P6.2.",
  "vectorsV2Shape": "The `vectorsV2` section (bd h76m.8, P3.1) pins the COMPOSITE + membership semantics both evaluators gained when they were rewired through normalizeToComposite: {all_of/any_of/none_of} groups, the includes/not_includes group-membership operators, unknown-operator fallback inside composites, and show_if-overrides-hidden for satisfied composites. Same case shape as `vectors`. The `require` section pins isFieldRequired (static required OR a satisfied require_if of either dialect; fail-open = NOT required). Static-required vector fields carry BOTH validation.required (runtime) and required (editor) so one expectation fits both islands.",
